<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Theoretical Justification</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a more formal theoretical underpinning for the GTD framework. We begin by framing the graph diffusion model within the lens of variational inference and then analyze the convergence properties of our proxy-guided synthesis process.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Variational Perspective of Graph Diffusion</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The generative process of denoising diffusion models can be rigorously justified as a procedure for optimizing the Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO) of the data’s log-likelihood.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO))<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a data point <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, a joint distribution <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(A_{0:T}|C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(A_{0:T}|C)</annotation></semantics></math>, and a variational posterior <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(A_{1:T}|A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(A_{1:T}|A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the ELBO for the conditional log-likelihood <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta}(A_{0}|C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta}(A_{0}|C)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbb{E}_{q(A_{1:T}|A_{0})}\left[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(A_{0:T}|C)}{q(A_{1:T}|A_{0})}\right]\leq\log p_{\theta}(A_{0}|C)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ELBO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbb{E}_{q(A_{1:T}|A_{0})}\left[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(A_{0:T}|C)}{q(A_{1:T}|A_{0})}\right]\leq\log p_{\theta}(A_{0}|C)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This lower bound can be decomposed into a series of terms that are more amenable to optimization:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\log p_{\theta}(A_{0}|A_{1},C)\right]-D_{KL}(q(A_{T}|A_{0})||p(A_{T}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\log p_{\theta}(A_{0}|A_{1},C)\right]-D_{KL}(q(A_{T}|A_{0})||p(A_{T}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{t=2}^{T}D_{KL}(q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})||p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{t=2}^{T}D_{KL}(q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})||p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Optimizing the ELBO involves minimizing the KL-divergence between the true posterior of the forward process and the learned reverse process. The forward process posterior is known to be tractable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Forward Process Posterior)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The posterior distribution <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is a Gaussian distribution given by:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})=\mathcal{N}\left(A_{t-1};\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0}),\tilde{\beta}_{t}\mathbf{I}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})=\mathcal{N}\left(A_{t-1};\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0}),\tilde{\beta}_{t}\mathbf{I}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0})=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝛍</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0})=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}_{t}=\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}_{t}=\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By parameterizing the reverse process <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C)</annotation></semantics></math> as a Gaussian whose mean is predicted by a neural network, we can connect the variational objective to a simpler, more practical training objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimality of the Denoising Objective)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming the reverse process <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C)</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian, minimizing the KL-divergence term <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{KL}(q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})||p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{KL}(q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})||p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C))</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#A3.E10" title="In C.1 Variational Perspective of Graph Diffusion ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Justification ‣ Dynamic Generation of Multi LLM Agents Communication Topologies with Graph Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> with respect to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to training a denoising network <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)</annotation></semantics></math> to predict <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing the L2 loss:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{simple}}=\mathbb{E}_{t,A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\left\|A_{0}-\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon,C,t)\right\|^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">simple</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{simple}}=\mathbb{E}_{t,A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\left\|A_{0}-\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon,C,t)\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our goal is to minimize the KL divergence between the true posterior and the learned reverse process:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{t}=D_{KL}(q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})||p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}=D_{KL}(q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})||p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Both distributions are Gaussian: <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})=\mathcal{N}(\cdot;\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0}),\tilde{\beta}_{t}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(A_{t-1}|A_{t},A_{0})=\mathcal{N}(\cdot;\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0}),\tilde{\beta}_{t}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C)=\mathcal{N}(\cdot;\bm{\mu}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(A_{t-1}|A_{t},C)=\mathcal{N}(\cdot;\bm{\mu}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we fix the variance of the reverse process to match the true posterior, <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}=\tilde{\beta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}=\tilde{\beta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The KL divergence between two multivariate Gaussians <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu_{1},\Sigma_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu_{1},\Sigma_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu_{2},\Sigma_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu_{2},\Sigma_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> simplifies when <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{1}=\Sigma_{2}=\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{1}=\Sigma_{2}=\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\|\mu_{1}-\mu_{2}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\|\mu_{1}-\mu_{2}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, minimizing the KL divergence is equivalent to minimizing the squared Euclidean distance between their means:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\frac{1}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\|\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0})-\bm{\mu}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\|^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\frac{1}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\|\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0})-\bm{\mu}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The expression for the true posterior mean is <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0})=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(A_{t},A_{0})=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We parameterize our model’s mean <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to have the same functional form, but predicting <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with our network <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into the loss function, the terms involving <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> cancel out:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\frac{1}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\left\|\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}-\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\frac{1}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}}\left\|\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}-\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\frac{(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t})^{2}}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})^{2}}\|A_{0}-\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\frac{(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\beta_{t})^{2}}{2\tilde{\beta}_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})^{2}}\|A_{0}-\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since the term outside the norm is a positive constant for a given timestep <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, minimizing <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to minimizing the simpler objective:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\|A_{0}-\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\|^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbb{E}_{A_{0},C,\epsilon}\left[\|A_{0}-\mathcal{G}_{\theta}(A_{t},C,t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">By substituting <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}A_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the expectation over all timesteps <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we arrive at the simplified loss function <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{simple}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>simple</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{simple}}</annotation></semantics></math> stated in the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Analysis of Proxy-Guided Synthesis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now analyze the role of the surrogate model and the ZO optimization step in guiding the synthesis towards high-reward topologies.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Accurate Surrogate Model)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A surrogate reward model <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate with respect to a true reward function <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,C)</annotation></semantics></math> if, for any valid topology <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and condition <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the approximation error is bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R(A,C)-\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)|\leq\epsilon_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R(A,C)-\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)|\leq\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The accuracy of this model directly bounds the sub-optimality of the topology generated by an ideal proxy-guided optimizer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Performance Gap Bound)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=\arg\max_{A}R(A,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=\arg\max_{A}R(A,C)</annotation></semantics></math> be the true optimal topology and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}=\arg\max_{A}\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}=\arg\max_{A}\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)</annotation></semantics></math> be the topology found by an ideal optimizer using an <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate proxy. The performance gap is bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A^{*},C)-R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\leq 2\epsilon_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A^{*},C)-R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\leq 2\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the maximizer of the proxy reward function, we have <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*},C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*},C)</annotation></semantics></math>. From the definition of an <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate surrogate model, we know that for any topology <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)-\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying this bound to <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)-\epsilon_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this with the optimality condition of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*},C)-\epsilon_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\geq\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*},C)-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Again, from the <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>-accuracy definition applied to <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can state that <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*},C)\geq R(A^{*},C)-\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A^{*},C)\geq R(A^{*},C)-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this into the previous inequality yields:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(R(A^{*},C)-\epsilon_{\max})-\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(R(A^{*},C)-\epsilon_{\max})-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=R(A^{*},C)-2\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=R(A^{*},C)-2\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging this final expression gives the desired bound:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A^{*},C)-R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\leq 2\epsilon_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A^{*},C)-R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)\leq 2\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Perfect Surrogate)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the surrogate model is perfect, i.e., <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\max}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\max}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then any topology <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{\text{proxy}}</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the proxy reward also maximizes the true reward, yielding <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)=R(A^{*},C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">proxy</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A^{*}_{\text{proxy}},C)=R(A^{*},C)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ZO-Guided Denoising Step)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">At a diffusion step <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, given the unguided prediction <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}=\mathcal{G}_{\theta^{*}}(A_{t},C,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}=\mathcal{G}_{\theta^{*}}(A_{t},C,t)</annotation></semantics></math>, the ZO-guided denoising step replaces <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">best</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}=\arg\max_{A\in\{A_{0,k}^{(t)}\}_{k=1}^{K}}\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">best</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}=\arg\max_{A\in\{A_{0,k}^{(t)}\}_{k=1}^{K}}\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and each candidate <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0,k}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0,k}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a discrete sample drawn from a distribution parameterized by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0,k}^{(t)}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(\sigma(\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0,k}^{(t)}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(\sigma(\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This ZO step can be viewed as approximating a gradient ascent step on the proxy reward landscape. Let <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\hat{A}_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{A\sim p(A|\hat{A}_{0})}[\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\hat{A}_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{A\sim p(A|\hat{A}_{0})}[\mathcal{P}_{\phi}(A,C)]</annotation></semantics></math>. The true gradient <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\hat{A}_{0}}J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\hat{A}_{0}}J</annotation></semantics></math> is intractable. The ZO step provides an update direction, <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}=A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}-\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>best</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}=A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}-\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which serves as a stochastic estimate of the ascent direction. The use of multiple samples (<math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>) reduces the variance of this estimate. The guided update for the next state <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is then computed using the posterior conditioned on <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>best</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0,\text{best}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{0}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, effectively biasing the sampling trajectory towards regions of higher proxy reward. This greedy, step-wise maximization provides a computationally efficient method for incorporating non-differentiable objectives directly into the generative process.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Supplementary Results</h2>

